			_html("<h2 id=troubleshooting>Troubleshooting</h2><h3>An override or a data-* variant class does nothing</h3><p>On the import distribution this is almost always the CSS entry: either the style layer was imported without <code>layer(components)</code>, or the matching <code>@custom-variant style-&lt;name&gt;</code> line is missing. Both fail silently — see <a href=#import-css>the import CSS entry</a> above.</p><h3>Components render unstyled</h3><p>On the copy distribution, this is almost always a missing Tailwind <code>@source</code> directive for your component directory. Tailwind v4 has to be told where your <code>.marko</code> files live, and needs a second directive if components were installed outside the directory the first one covers.</p><h3>\"Cannot find module\" for a @zag-js package</h3><p><code>marko-ui add</code> installs a component's declared dependencies automatically. If you copied files manually instead, install them yourself — the list is in the component's registry JSON under <code>dependencies</code>.</p><h3>Serialization errors on interaction</h3><p>A Zag service or API object escaped into reactive state. This is a component-authoring mistake rather than an installation problem — see <a href=/docs/creating-components>Creating Components</a> for the rule and the fix.</p>");
